<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Unit 1 — Present perfect &amp; Use your English — Play — Friday B2</title>
<style>
  :root{
    --green:#6BAE2E;
    --green-dark:#4d8120;
    --ink:#1a1a1a;
    --bg:#ffffff;
    --char-a:#0F7B6C;
    --char-b:#6B3FA0;
    --char-c:#C2540A;
    --char-d:#1D6FB8;
  }
  *{box-sizing:border-box;}
  body{
    margin:0;
    font-family:-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    background:var(--bg);
    color:var(--ink);
  }
  header{
    display:flex;
    justify-content:space-between;
    align-items:flex-end;
    padding:24px 40px;
    border-bottom:4px solid var(--green);
    flex-wrap:wrap;
    gap:16px;
  }
  .logo{display:flex;align-items:flex-end;gap:11px;}
  .logo .word{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-weight:800;font-size:33pt;letter-spacing:-1.2px;line-height:.9;color:#6BAE2E;}
  .logo .lc{font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-weight:700;font-size:8.5pt;letter-spacing:2.5px;line-height:1.18;padding-bottom:4px;color:#4d8120;}
  .title-block{text-align:right;}
  .title-block h1{margin:0;font-size:24px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);}
  .title-block p{margin:6px 0 0;font-size:15px;color:#555;letter-spacing:.5px;text-transform:uppercase;}

  .toggle-bar{
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    gap:20px;
    padding:22px 20px 6px;
    flex-wrap:wrap;
  }
  .toggle-btn{
    font-size:18px;
    font-weight:700;
    padding:14px 28px;
    border-radius:12px;
    border:3px solid var(--green);
    background:#fff;
    color:var(--green-dark);
    cursor:pointer;
    transition:all .15s ease;
    font-family:inherit;
  }
  .toggle-btn:hover{background:#EAF4DA;}
  .toggle-btn.active{background:var(--green);color:#fff;}

  .cast-bar{
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    gap:24px;
    padding:16px 20px 6px;
    flex-wrap:wrap;
  }
  .cast-pill{
    font-size:15px;
    font-weight:700;
    padding:8px 18px;
    border-radius:30px;
    border:2px solid;
    background:#fff;
  }
  .cast-pill.char-a{color:var(--char-a);border-color:var(--char-a);}
  .cast-pill.char-b{color:var(--char-b);border-color:var(--char-b);}
  .cast-pill.char-c{color:var(--char-c);border-color:var(--char-c);}
  .cast-pill.char-d{color:var(--char-d);border-color:var(--char-d);}

  .scene-setup{
    max-width:900px;
    margin:14px auto 0;
    padding:0 24px;
    text-align:center;
    font-size:19px;
    color:#444;
    font-style:italic;
  }
  .focus-tags{
    max-width:900px;
    margin:10px auto 0;
    padding:0 24px;
    text-align:center;
    font-size:14px;
    color:#6BAE2E;
    font-weight:700;
    letter-spacing:.4px;
    text-transform:uppercase;
  }

  main{max-width:960px;margin:0 auto;padding:30px 24px 40px;}
  .cast-version{display:none;}
  .cast-version.active{display:block;}

  .line{
    display:flex;
    gap:24px;
    align-items:baseline;
    margin-bottom:26px;
    padding-bottom:26px;
    border-bottom:1px solid #eee;
  }
  .line:last-child{border-bottom:none;}
  .char-name{
    flex:0 0 130px;
    font-size:20px;
    font-weight:800;
    text-transform:uppercase;
    letter-spacing:.5px;
  }
  .char-a .char-name{color:var(--char-a);}
  .char-b .char-name{color:var(--char-b);}
  .char-c .char-name{color:var(--char-c);}
  .char-d .char-name{color:var(--char-d);}
  .line-text{
    font-size:26px;
    line-height:1.5;
    flex:1;
  }
  .line-text b{color:var(--green-dark);font-weight:800;}
  .stage-direction{
    font-size:18px;
    color:#777;
    font-style:italic;
    text-align:center;
    margin:22px 0;
  }

  .cast-note{
    max-width:900px;
    margin:10px auto 40px;
    padding:16px 22px;
    border:1.5px dashed #cfcfcf;
    border-radius:10px;
    font-size:14px;
    color:#666;
    line-height:1.6;
  }
  .cast-note b{color:var(--ink);}

  footer{
    text-align:center;
    padding:24px;
    font-size:14px;
    color:#888;
    border-top:2px solid #eee;
  }

  @media print{
    .toggle-bar{display:none !important;}
  }

  @media (max-width:700px){
    header{flex-direction:column;align-items:center;text-align:center;}
    .title-block{text-align:center;}
    .line{flex-direction:column;gap:6px;}
    .char-name{flex-basis:auto;font-size:17px;}
    .line-text{font-size:22px;}
    .toggle-btn{font-size:15px;padding:11px 18px;}
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <div class="logo"><span class="word">Somerset</span><span class="lc">LANGUAGE<br>CENTRE</span></div>
  <div class="title-block">
    <h1>Unit 1 — Present perfect &amp; Use your English</h1>
    <p>Play &middot; Friday B2</p>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="toggle-bar">
  <button class="toggle-btn active" id="btnTrio" onclick="showVersion('trio')">Trio &middot; Ainhoa, Sonia, Luc&iacute;a</button>
  <button class="toggle-btn" id="btnQuartet" onclick="showVersion('quartet')">Group of 4 &middot; Elena, Marta, Valeria, Zoe</button>
</div>

<!-- ================= TRIO VERSION ================= -->
<div class="cast-version active" id="version-trio">
  <div class="cast-bar">
    <span class="cast-pill char-a">Ainhoa</span>
    <span class="cast-pill char-b">Sonia</span>
    <span class="cast-pill char-c">Luc&iacute;a</span>
  </div>
  <p class="scene-setup">A caf&eacute; terrace in Ruzafa, three weeks after summer camp ended.</p>
  <p class="focus-tags">Present perfect simple &amp; continuous &middot; phrasal verbs &middot; prepositions (p.13)</p>
  <main>
    <div class="line char-a"><div class="char-name">Ainhoa</div><div class="line-text">I've <b>missed</b> you both so much! I <b>haven't seen</b> you since the summer camp.</div></div>
    <div class="line char-b"><div class="char-name">Sonia</div><div class="line-text">I know! I've <b>been thinking</b> about you all week actually &mdash; I've only just <b>got back</b> from my aunt's in Alicante.</div></div>
    <div class="line char-c"><div class="char-name">Luc&iacute;a</div><div class="line-text">Wait, have you two <b>fallen out</b> or something? You've been weird with each other since June.</div></div>
    <div class="line char-a"><div class="char-name">Ainhoa</div><div class="line-text">No! Actually we've <b>hit it off</b> more than ever this summer &mdash; we've <b>been messaging</b> every day.</div></div>
    <div class="line char-b"><div class="char-name">Sonia</div><div class="line-text">True. Although her little brother has <b>stood me up</b> for a video call three times this week, so I've kind of <b>gone off</b> him.</div></div>
    <div class="stage-direction">Lucía laughs and picks up the menu.</div>
    <div class="line char-c"><div class="char-name">Luc&iacute;a</div><div class="line-text">Classic. Anyway &mdash; has anyone read anything interesting these holidays? I've just finished a book about music and the brain. Apparently when you <b>concentrate on</b> a new song, your brain is constantly predicting what's coming, and getting it right can <b>cheer</b> you <b>up</b> instantly.</div></div>
    <div class="line char-a"><div class="char-name">Ainhoa</div><div class="line-text">That's amazing &mdash; I've <b>never</b> really thought about it before. Sharing stuff like that really <b>leads to</b> stronger friendships, don't you think?</div></div>
    <div class="line char-b"><div class="char-name">Sonia</div><div class="line-text">Definitely. I nearly <b>burst into</b> tears at a concert this summer for no reason &mdash; maybe that's why!</div></div>
    <div class="line char-c"><div class="char-name">Luc&iacute;a</div><div class="line-text">Right, I haven't eaten since breakfast and it's <b>getting</b> me <b>down</b>. Shall we order?</div></div>
    <div class="line char-a"><div class="char-name">Ainhoa</div><div class="line-text">Let's <b>chill out</b> here a bit first. We haven't had a proper catch-up in ages.</div></div>
  </main>
</div>

<!-- ================= GROUP OF 4 VERSION ================= -->
<div class="cast-version" id="version-quartet">
  <div class="cast-bar">
    <span class="cast-pill char-a">Elena</span>
    <span class="cast-pill char-b">Marta</span>
    <span class="cast-pill char-c">Valeria</span>
    <span class="cast-pill char-d">Zoe</span>
  </div>
  <p class="scene-setup">Cycling along the Turia gardens on a Sunday afternoon.</p>
  <p class="focus-tags">Present perfect simple &amp; continuous &middot; phrasal verbs &middot; prepositions (p.13)</p>
  <main>
    <div class="line char-a"><div class="char-name">Elena</div><div class="line-text">I can't believe it's <b>been</b> three weeks since school finished &mdash; I've <b>missed</b> the Turia gardens so much.</div></div>
    <div class="line char-b"><div class="char-name">Marta</div><div class="line-text">Me too! Zoe, have you <b>ever cycled</b> here before? It's basically the whole city on one bike path.</div></div>
    <div class="line char-d"><div class="char-name">Zoe</div><div class="line-text"><b>Never</b> &mdash; I only moved here in September, remember? But I've <b>already fallen</b> in love with it. Everyone's been so welcoming, we <b>hit it off</b> straight away.</div></div>
    <div class="line char-c"><div class="char-name">Valeria</div><div class="line-text">Aw, we're glad you joined! Although Elena's <b>been getting</b> me <b>down</b> all summer complaining about her phone.</div></div>
    <div class="line char-a"><div class="char-name">Elena</div><div class="line-text">Because it broke and I <b>still haven't fixed</b> it! I've <b>been relying</b> on Marta for everything.</div></div>
    <div class="line char-b"><div class="char-name">Marta</div><div class="line-text">True, and honestly it's starting to <b>get</b> me <b>down</b> too, ha. Anyway, has anyone read that article about music and the brain?</div></div>
    <div class="line char-d"><div class="char-name">Zoe</div><div class="line-text">Yes! It said your brain <b>concentrates on</b> predicting the next note, and when it's right, it gives you a little reward &mdash; that's why a good song can <b>cheer</b> you <b>up</b> instantly.</div></div>
    <div class="line char-c"><div class="char-name">Valeria</div><div class="line-text">That explains why I nearly <b>burst into</b> tears at the fireworks concert in July &mdash; the music just got to me.</div></div>
    <div class="stage-direction">Elena checks her watch.</div>
    <div class="line char-a"><div class="char-name">Elena</div><div class="line-text">Sharing stuff like that really <b>leads to</b> stronger friendships, I think. Right, shall we get going before it gets dark?</div></div>
    <div class="line char-b"><div class="char-name">Marta</div><div class="line-text">Wait &mdash; don't <b>stand</b> us <b>up</b> like last time! You said that in June and then you never showed up.</div></div>
    <div class="line char-a"><div class="char-name">Elena</div><div class="line-text">I promise! I <b>haven't stood</b> anyone <b>up</b> since&hellip; well, since June.</div></div>
  </main>
</div>

<div class="cast-note">
  <b>Teacher's note (not for students).</b> Two full, different scripts &mdash; not the same scene with names swapped &mdash; because the group is now seven (Zoe joined 25 Sep 2026): the established trio (Ainhoa, Sonia, Luc&iacute;a) performs one, and the group of four (Elena, Marta, Valeria, Zoe) performs the other, so both groups run their own play in the same class rather than repeating one script. Both versions drill present perfect simple/continuous with the SB p.12 adverbs (already, still, yet, just, ever, never, before) and all seven p.13 phrasal verbs (go off, cheer up, chill out, hit it off, fall out, get down, stand up) plus four of the p.13 prepositions (lead to, concentrate on, responsible for &rarr; implied via "relying on", burst into). The Valorie Salimpoor open-cloze passage (music predicting the brain's reward response) is referenced in both scenes as a natural bridge into the Exam Task, paraphrased rather than quoted. Zoe's line in the quartet places her as an established member of the group, not a guest.
</div>

<footer>Somerset Language Centre &middot; Val&egrave;ncia &middot; Friday B2 &middot; Unit 1</footer>

<script>
function showVersion(v){
  document.getElementById('version-trio').classList.toggle('active', v==='trio');
  document.getElementById('version-quartet').classList.toggle('active', v==='quartet');
  document.getElementById('btnTrio').classList.toggle('active', v==='trio');
  document.getElementById('btnQuartet').classList.toggle('active', v==='quartet');
}
</script>
</body>
</html>
